---

import {Image} from 'astro:assets';

import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import ActionButton from "@components/buttons/ActionButton.astro";
import PurchaseButton from "@components/buttons/PurchaseButton.astro";
import BHLogomark from "@assets/images/BisectHostingLogomark.svg"
import PioneerHero from "@assets/images/Hosting/PioneerHero.png"
import SimTweeney from "@assets/images/Hosting/20260708202033_1.jpg"
import FactoryImage2 from "@assets/images/Hosting/20260708201539_1.jpg"
import FactoryImage3 from "@assets/images/Hosting/20260708200710_1.jpg"
import FactoryImage4 from "@assets/images/Hosting/20260708200253_1.jpg"
import DNSSymbol from "@assets/images/MaterialIcons/dns_24dp_FFFFFF_FILL1_wght400_GRAD0_opsz24.svg"

---

<Layout title="SpaceGameDev / Hosting">

	<div id="header-spacer" class="h-12.5 mb-10"/>

	<div class="m-auto w-[90%] 2xl:w-[80%] font-bh-sans">

		<div id="heading" class="mt-12.5 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 items-center">

			<div class="lg:order-last lg:ml-auto lg:mr-0">
				<Image
						src={BHLogomark}
						alt="SpaceGameDev"
						width="512"
						height="512"
						loading="eager"
						class="w-30 lg:w-sm xl:w-md 2xl:w-lg mb-4 2xl:m-none xl:animate-breathe"
				/>
			</div>

			<div class="leading-3">
				<h1 class="font-bh-heading font-bold text-white xl:text-6xl lg:text-5xl md:text-4xl text-3xl">Satisfactory Server Hosting</h1><br/>
				<h2 class="font-bh-heading text-bh-new-car lg:text-4xl text-3xl"> With<br/>Bisect<br class="md:hidden"/>Hosting </h2><br/>
				<p class="text-white text-2xl bg-[#101014]/25 backdrop-blur-sm p-2">
					On this page I'll explain how BisectHosting can improve your Modded Satisfactory multiplayer experience!
				</p>

				<br/>

				<div class="flex flex-wrap place-content-center gap-2 w-fit mr-10">

					<ActionButton
							link="#interested"
							title="Get Started Now"
							variant="bh_secondary"
							target="_self"
					/>

					<ActionButton
							link="#why-bh"
							title="Why BH?"
							variant="bh_primary"
							target="_self"
					/>

				</div>

			</div>


			<script>
				import { animate } from "motion"

				document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
					animate("#heading", { y: [225, 0], opacity: [0, 100] }, { ease: "easeInOut", duration: 1} )

				});
			</script>

		</div>

		<div id="why-bh"/>

		<br/><br/>
		<br/><br/>

		<div class="w-fit m-auto bg-[#101014]/25 backdrop-blur-sm p-5">
			<p class="font-bold text-3xl font-heading m-auto w-fit md:text-center text-bh-vivid-sky-blue"> All screenshots on this page were taken of factories built on my BisectHosting server. </p>
		</div>

		<br/><br/>
		<br/><br/>

		<h2 class="lg:text-5xl text-3xl font-bold m-auto w-fit text-bh-white font-bh-heading text-center"> Our relationship </h2>

		<br/><br/>

		<div class="grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-rows-1 grid-cols-1 auto-rows-min">

			<div class="border  border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border p-5">
				<p class="text-white text-xl text-left m-auto w-fit">
					I'm a big advocate for self-hosting as much as possible, but I've always found hosting game servers to be a pain.<br/><br/>
					When I started looking at managed hosting providers, BisectHosting was one of the first I came across.<br/><br/>
					What I liked most when I tried them is that I don't have to deal with port forwarding anymore, and updating the server is one click, no SSH needed.<br/><br/>
					In 2024, I decided to officially partner with them, meaning they sponsor me and provide me with a server to develop on for free,
					and I can save you money when you sign up!
				</p>
			</div>

			<Image
					src={SimTweeney}
					alt="Sim Tweeney and Vase Jarlet admire their factory"
					class="border  border-white/10 md:self-center"
			/>

		</div>

		<br/><br/>

		<h2 class="lg:text-5xl text-3xl font-bold m-auto w-fit text-bh-white font-bh-heading text-center"> How that benefits you </h2>

		<br/><br/>

		<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-5 grid-rows-6 grid-cols-1 grid-flow-col m-auto w-fit">

			<Image
					src={FactoryImage2}
					alt="NotSpace and Biko drink coffee while watching the battery factory"
					class="hidden lg:block border  border-white/10 row-span-3 self-center"
			/>

			<Image
					src={FactoryImage3}
					alt="My main base in the Grass Fields"
					class="hidden lg:block border  border-white/10 row-span-3 self-center"
			/>

			<!--

			<Image
					src={FactoryImage4}
					alt="The factory producing Nuclear Fuel Rods for my Nuclear Power Plants"
					class="hidden lg:block border  border-white/10 row-span-2"
					width="800"
			/>

			-->

			<!--

			<div class="border  border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border p-5 w-full col-span-2 2xl:row-span-2 row-span-3 order-1 max-w-200">

				<ul class="text-white text-xl/10 text-left m-5 w-fit list-disc">
					<li>All of my mods are designed to work great on dedicated servers. <br/> <span class="text-gray-400 text-sm">(Thanks in part to BH providing me the resources to test them!)</span></li>
					<li>As many friends as you want; While you're typically limited to 4 players, you can have as many as you want with a BisectHosting server!</li>
					<li>Servers are super simple to set up.</li>
					<li>No port-forwarding or SSH needed.</li>
					<li>Choose any of the 20+ locations across the globe closest to you for the best latency.</li>
					<li>Large modded saves are much easier to manage, since they stay centralized in one location.</li>
					<li>The Satisfactory Mod Manager has built-in support to install mods on dedicated servers.</li>
					<li>Game updates are easy to install, and so are mods (Assuming Coffee Stain doesn't update the engine and break mods <b><i>again</i></b>.)</li>
					<li>If updates do break mods, your server will continue to work fine in vanilla until we can update our mods. <br/> <span class="text-gray-400 text-sm">(Though you will likely need to uninstall them temporarily.)</span></li>
					<li>If you get bored of Satisfactory, you can just swap your server to any of the other 100+ games BH hosts.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			-->

			<div class="border  border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border p-5 order-1 text-bh-white text-xl">
				All of my mods are designed to work great on dedicated servers, in part because I'm able to test more easily using the server they provide me!
			</div>

			<div class="border  border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border p-5 order-1 text-bh-white text-xl">
				While you're typically limited to 4 players, you can have as many as you want with a BisectHosting server!
				Just make sure to select a plan with enough memory to make it a smooth experience for everyone.
			</div>

			<div class="border  border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border p-5 order-1 text-bh-white text-xl">
				Servers are super simple to set up, no port-forwarding or SSH needed!<br/>
				Plus, the Satisfactory Mod Manager has built-in support to easily install mods on dedicated servers!
			</div>

			<div class="border  border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border p-5 order-1 text-bh-white text-xl">
				There are over 20 server locations across the globe for you to choose from to ensure you get the lowest latency!
			</div>

			<div class="border  border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border p-5 order-1 text-bh-white text-xl">
				Both the game and mods are simple to update (Assuming Coffee Stain doesn't update the engine and break mods <b><i>again</i></b>.)
				If updates do break mods, your server will continue to work fine in vanilla until we can update our mods. <br/> <span class="text-gray-400 text-sm">(Though you will likely need to uninstall them temporarily.)</span>
			</div>

			<div class="border  border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border p-5 order-1 text-bh-white text-xl">
				If you get bored of Satisfactory, you can just swap your server to any of the other 100+ games BH hosts!
			</div>

		</div>

		<br/><br/>
		<Image
				src={FactoryImage4}
				alt="The factory producing Nuclear Fuel Rods for my Nuclear Power Plants"
				class="lg:hidden border  border-white/10"
				width="800"
		/>

		<br/><br/>

		<h2 class="lg:text-5xl text-3xl font-bold m-auto w-fit text-bh-white font-bh-heading text-center"> Support </h2>

		<br/><br/>

		<div class="border  border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border p-5 w-full max-w-250 text-bh-white m-auto">
			<p class="text-white text-xl text-left m-auto w-fit">
				If you have any issues, trained professionals who understand modded servers are ready to help,
				all day and night, any day of the year.<br/>
				You'll usually get a response back within 15 minutes.<br/><br/>

				<ActionButton link="https://help.bisecthosting.com/" target="_blank" title="Help Center" variant="bh_primary"/><br/><br/>

				There's also Biko to assist you with quick issues that don't need a human involved,
				and a vast knowledgebase available covering virtually any topic regarding your server.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div id="interested"/>

		<br/><br/>

		<h2 class="lg:text-5xl text-3xl font-bold m-auto w-fit text-bh-white font-bh-heading text-center"> Interested? </h2>

		<br/><br/>

		<div class="border border-white/10  bg-bh-eerie-black box-border grid md:grid-cols-2  w-full max-w-250 m-auto">

			<Image
					src={PioneerHero}
					alt="A Pioneer gesturing at another Pioneer giving a thumbs up"
					width="300"
					class="md:ml-5 md:mt-5 order-last md:order-0 md:mr-0 md:mb-0 m-auto"
			/>

			<div class="self-center m-5">

				<p class="text-white text-xl text-left m-auto w-fit">
					All you need to do is click the link below and use promo code "<code class="font-mono text-bh-vivid-sky-blue">SPACEGAMEDEV</code>" at checkout to get 25% off!<br/>
					<code class="text-gray-400 font-sans text-base">This also benefits me, as I earn a commission from sales made when using my link, which goes towards maintaining my existing mods and creating new ones for you to enjoy!</code><br/>
				</p>

				<br/>

				<div class="m-auto">
					<PurchaseButton title="Create Server" image={DNSSymbol} alt="DNS" link="https://bisecthosting.com/spacegamedev?r=PostOverhaulWebsiteHostingPage"/>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

	</div>

</Layout>